-- title:
--   Inertia at a supersingular point is H/⟨-1⟩
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, an integer $M\ge 5$ with $p\nmid M$, a field $L$ of characteristic zero that is a $p$-cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$, and a primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta\in L$. Let $K_1$ be the $L$-subfield of $L((q))$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion field [`ModularCurve.x1x0FunctionFieldC ℚ M p`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L142) attached to $\Gamma_1(M)\cap\Gamma_0(p)$, and $K_2$ the corresponding subfield built from [`ModularCurve.qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ (CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma0 (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L101), with $K_2\le K_1$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, with $p$ in its maximal ideal, with $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, with uniformiser $\varpi$ generating that maximal ideal, and with compatible algebra structures on $K_1$ and $K_2$; let $j\in K_1$ and $j_2\in K_2$ be nonzero elements whose Laurent series are the image of the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157). Assume given a morphism $\pi_2$ from the two-chart integral model [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K₁ j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) (the pushout gluing the spectra of the algebras of elements integral over $A[j]$ and over $A[j^{-1}]$) to the model over $K_2$ built from $j_2$, together with an $A$-algebra map $\iota_{F_2}$ of finite charts compatible with the inclusions of Laurent series, commuting with the structure morphisms to $\operatorname{Spec} A$ and with the finite-chart immersions, with $\pi_2^{-1}$ of the finite chart the finite chart, with $\pi_2$ and $\iota_{F_2}$ finite, and with the finite chart of $K_1$ consisting exactly of the elements integral over the image of $\iota_{F_2}$. Let $z$ be a point of the model such that the germ at $z$ of the global section coming from $\varpi$ lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk, let $y$ be a point of the finite chart $\operatorname{Spec}$ mapping to $z$, and assume $y$ is supersingular: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $p$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from the finite chart algebra to $\Omega$ with kernel the prime of $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet p Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), that is, every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has no nonzero point killed by $p$. Let $G$ be a finite group acting faithfully on $K_1$ by ring automorphisms, fixing every element of $K_1$ whose Laurent series lies in $K_2$ and having exactly those elements as invariants, and acting on the finite chart algebra compatibly with its action on $K_1$; let $\mathfrak{y}$ be the prime ideal of $y$. Then there is a subgroup $H\le(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ containing $-1$ such that every $h\in H$ satisfies $h^2-th+1=0$ in $\mathbb{Z}/M$ for some $t\in\{-2,-1,0,1,2\}$, with $t=2$ forcing $h=1$ and $t=-2$ forcing $h=-1$, and such that there exists a group isomorphism between $H/\langle -1\rangle$ and the inertia subgroup `𝔶.inertia G` of $G$ at $\mathfrak{y}$.
--
--   This is the Katz–Mazur description of the inertia of the diamond action at a supersingular point of the special fibre of the integral model of $X(\Gamma_1(M)\cap\Gamma_0(p))$: the inertia group is $H/\{\pm 1\}$ for a subgroup $H$ of $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ whose elements satisfy a quadratic trace relation with trace of absolute value at most $2$, which bounds its order by $3$. It is used by the two companion results treating the wild cases $p=3$ and $p=2$, where cyclicity of the inertia group and the fact that its order is not divisible by $p$ are extracted from these relations.
